\begin_layout Subsection
Project aims
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The main objective of this doctoral project was to develop the skills required
 to prepare thin cross sections of fragile crystalline material such that
 they could be characterised by high resolution scanning transmission electron
 microscopy (STEM).
 Subsequently, this technique was applied to a range of novel van der Waals'
 structures to reveal the nature of buried interfaces and defects.
 Image processing methods were then developed to extract quantitative informatio
n from the STEM images.
 This progression is summarised in Figure 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "fig:Overview_Thesis"

\end_inset

.
\end_layout

