 This holds all of the elastically scattered electrons and is the most intense
 feature in the spectrum if the sample is suitably thin.
 Next is the plasmon peak and, together with the zero loss peak, allows
 calculation of the mean free path of electrons through the specimen.
 After these come the core-loss edges.
 These come in a variety of characteristic shapes and at different energies.
 For example, the oxygen K-edge shows a simple sharp onset whilst the Ba-M
 edge is composed of two sharp peaks comprising the M
\begin_inset script subscript

\begin_layout Plain Layout
4
\end_layout

\end_inset

