\begin_layout Subsection
Summary
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This literature review has outlined the motivation to characterise the propertie
s of heterostructures fabricated from graphene and other 2D materials, particula
rly the buried interfaces within these structures where the materials meet.
 One of the few ways of acheiving this is by cross section STEM imaging.
 This requires preparation of thin lamellae extracted from the substrate
 and polished to electron-transparency using a FIB dual-beam instrument.
 The theory to optimise the final FIB polishing procedure has been outlined.
 STEM imaging of 2D materials in both plan view and cross section has been
 reviewed, as well as the techniques surrounding STEM analysis and the problems
 associated with electron beam damage in these sensitive materials.
\end_layout

