 basal planes up to one van der Waals bond range (~ 2 – 6 Å) from the TMDC
 layer and hence calculate the interlayer separation between this and the
 transition metal plane within the TMDC layer.
 The distance between the nearest hBN peak and the TMDC peak can then be
 measured across all equivalent interfaces and an average value determined
 considering interlayer spacing both above and below the TMDC layer.
